ifferential_b3cc353a_010_curated20261027_002","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"conceptual","question":"Let $f$ be differentiable at $x$ and let $\\mathrm{d}x\\neq0$ be an increment. Which quantity is the differential $\\mathrm{d}f(x)$?","options":["$f(x+\\mathrm{d}x)-f(x)$, the rise of the graph over the step","$f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, the rise of the tangent line over the step","$f(x)+f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, the height of the tangent line at $x+\\mathrm{d}x$","$f'(x)$, the slope of the tangent line at $x$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"318c7672b5d1a12fea6a4c95","time_limit":35},{"id":"year_1_1a_math_i_calculus_differential_b3cc353a_topup20261028_001","difficulty":"standard","question_type":"application","question":"Let $f(x)=x^2$, let $x\\in\\mathbb{R}$ and let $\\mathrm{d}x\\neq0$. With $\\Delta f=f(x+\\mathrm{d}x)-f(x)$ and the differential $\\mathrm{d}f(x)=f'(x)\\,\\mathrm{d}x$, what is $\\Delta f-\\mathrm{d}f(x)$?","options":["$0$, for every increment $\\mathrm{d}x$","$(\\mathrm{d}x)^2$","$-(\\mathrm{d}x)^2$","$(\\mathrm{d}x)^2$ for $\\mathrm{d}x>0$ and $-(\\mathrm{d}x)^2$ for $\\mathrm{d}x<0$"],"answer_mode":"server","feedback_revision":"f1f942588dccb03230043597","time_limit":35}]}}